-## The core principle
+## 核心原则
 
-> **Never wait for a full CI run before addressing review comments.** A comment fix pushes a new commit that re-triggers CI anyway, so handling comments *while CI is still running* collapses the two timelines instead of serializing them. Handle comments first; if that pass pushed, the old CI failure is against a dead SHA — skip it and let the new run start.
+> **在处理评论评论之前，永远不要等待完整的CI运行。**评论修复会推送一个重新触发CI的新提交，因此在CI仍在运行时*处理评论会折叠两个时间线，而不是序列化它们。先处理评论；如果该传递被推送，则旧的 CI 失败是针对死 SHA 的 - 跳过它并让新的运行开始。
 >
-> **The same rule applies to an in-progress review.** Act on the feedback a reviewer has *already posted* rather than waiting for its 👀/"reviewing" signal to clear — the in-progress signal gates only the "looks ready" call (Step 3), never the work. Waiting for a review to finish before resolving the comments it already left serializes exactly the way waiting for CI would.
+> **同样的规则适用于正在进行的审核。** 根据审核者*已经发布*的反馈采取行动，而不是等待其👀/“审核”信号清除 - 进行中信号仅控制“看起来准备好”调用（第 3 步），而不是工作。在解决已留下的评论之前等待审核完成，其序列化方式与等待 CI 的方式完全相同。
 
-## Pre-authorization and delegate scope
+## 预授权及委托范围
 
-**Before any write** (rerun, or a delegated push/reply), the delegated skills re-validate against remote, and before a push they also confirm the PR is still open. A local state lock does not prevent a second babysitter or a human from having acted, so never assume the snapshot is still current at mutation time. `ce-resolve-pr-feedback` and `ce-debug` perform their own commit/push/reply/resolve mutations; this skill only orchestrates, records, and reports.
+**在任何写入之前**（重新运行或委派 push/reply），委派技能会针对远程重新验证，并且在推送之前，它们还会确认 PR 仍处于打开状态。本地状态锁不会阻止第二个PR 看护或人类采取行动，因此永远不要假设快照在突变时仍然是当前的。 `ce-resolve-pr-feedback`和`ce-debug`执行自己的commit/push/reply/resolve突变；这个技能只是编排、记录和报告。
 
-**Running the babysitter pre-authorizes those mutations.** The loop commits, pushes, replies, and resolves review threads as its normal operation — never pause to ask the user to approve any of them. For a confirmed managed stack, the manager-owned clean upstack rebase and recoverable `gh stack push` after a target mutation are likewise implicit in being asked to babysit that layer; leaving dependents knowingly based on the old target would violate the managed-stack contract. A general "confirm before pushing or opening PRs" instruction governs your own ad-hoc actions, not the loop's authorized mutations — gating them on a user prompt is not caution, it is the loop silently ceasing to babysit. The only things the loop ever hands to the user are: the **final merge** decision under `target`/`stack-ready` (print the exact `gh stack merge <N> --yes --squash` command when ready-as-next and not auto-merging); a **`needs-human`** residual it deliberately did not decide (including an aborted stack conflict); and the **blocked-external** handback (Step 3). Under `stack-land` the prefix merge after settle is one of the authorized changes. Everything else — fixing a failing check, resolving a convergent review thread, pushing the fix, propagating it through a confirmed managed upstack, replying and resolving the thread, refreshing a PR description that incremental changes made stale — it does itself, without asking.
+**运行PR 看护会预先授权这些突变。**循环会像正常操作一样提交、推送、回复和解析审核线程——永远不要停下来要求用户批准其中任何一个。对于已确认的托管堆栈，管理者拥有的清理堆栈变基和目标突变后可恢复的`gh stack push`同样隐含在被要求照顾该层；故意根据旧目标留下依赖者将违反托管堆栈合同。一般的“在推送或打开 PRs 之前确认”指令控制您自己的临时操作，而不是循环的授权突变 - 在用户提示上对它们进行门控并不是谨慎，而是循环默默地停止照顾。循环交给用户的唯一东西是： `target`/`stack-ready` 下的 **最终合并** 决定（在准备下一步时打印确切的 `gh stack merge <N> --yes --squash` 命令，而不是自动合并）； **`needs-human`** 故意没有决定的残差（包括中止的堆栈冲突）；和 **受阻外部** 回传（步骤 3）。在`stack-land`下，解决后的前缀合并是授权的更改之一。其他一切 - 修复失败的检查，解决收敛审查线程，推送修复，通过已确认的托管堆栈传播它，回复并解决线程，刷新增量更改过时的PR描述 - 它会自行完成，无需询问。
 
-**The authority you pass down is bounded, not blanket.** `ce-resolve-pr-feedback` and `ce-debug` mutate under *your* inherited authorization, not because being invoked is itself authority. The scope you carry to them: **target** = this PR's head; **actions** = fix / commit / push / reply / resolve; **exclusions** = merge (unless this run is `stack-land` and the merge is the caller-owned stack-land step after settle), rebase, force-push, approve-CI; **origin** = the user's babysit invocation. A delegate may *narrow* this (decline a fix, defer a `needs-human`) but must **never broaden** it — a `ce-debug` pass whose only "fix" is a rebase or force-push is outside what babysitting authorizes and comes back as a `needs-human` residual, not applied. Step 7's `gh stack` transaction stays with this skill and occurs only after a delegate reports a pushed target; it is not part of either delegate's scope. The `stack-land` merge+sync step likewise stays with this skill after settle — never delegated to `ce-resolve`/`ce-debug`. Harnesses do not reliably carry a scope in-band, so the exclusions are the boundary *you* enforce when composing a delegate's result: reject and re-report any result that performed an excluded action.
+**你传递下来的权限是有限的，而不是一揽子的。** `ce-resolve-pr-feedback`和`ce-debug`在*你的*继承的授权下发生变异，而不是因为被调用本身就是权限。你携带给他们的范围： **目标** = 这个PR的头； **操作** = 修复/提交/推送/回复/解决； **排除** = 合并（除非此运行为 `stack-land` 并且合并是结算后调用者拥有的堆栈着陆步骤）、变基、强制推送、批准-CI； **起源** = 用户的PR 看护调用。代表可以“缩小”这个范围（拒绝修复，推迟`needs-human`），但绝不能扩大**它——唯一“修复”是变基或强制推送的`ce-debug`通行证超出了PR 看护授权的范围，并作为`needs-human`残差返回，未应用。第 7 步的`gh stack`交易仍然使用此技能，并且仅在委托报告推送目标之后发生；它不属于任何一个代表的范围。 `stack-land`合并+同步步骤同样在解决后保留此技能 - 从未委托给`ce-resolve`/`ce-debug`。宿主不能可靠地承载带内范围，因此排除是*您*在编写委托结果时强制执行的边界：拒绝并重新报告执行排除操作的任何结果。
 
-**Pre-authorization is not deafness.** A live user instruction during the run — "stop pushing," "leave CI alone," "only reply, don't resolve" — immediately narrows, redirects, or revokes what the loop may change. Re-evaluate the remaining work against it before the next mutation. The live instruction supersedes the standing authorization, and unlike the settle/keep-going decisions it is never something you have to ask for — you just honor it when it arrives.
+**预授权不是充耳不闻。** 运行期间的实时用户指令 - “停止推送”、“单独留下 CI”、“仅回复，不解决” - 立即缩小、重定向或撤销循环可能更改的内容。在下一次突变之前重新评估剩余的工作。实时指令取代了长期授权，与settle/keep-going决定不同，它永远不是你必须要求的东西——你只需在它到达时尊重它即可。
