-# Step 1 detail: forge check, PR resolution, chain classification, checkout, watch mode
+# 步骤一详情：伪造检查、PR解析、链分类、结账、观看模式
 
-## Prerequisites
+## 先决条件
 
-The loop runs `gh`, `git`, and a bundled Python helper against a local checkout with filesystem access. A harness without those (some sandboxed GUI environments) cannot run this skill — say so and stop rather than half-running.
+该循环针对具有文件系统访问权限的本地结帐运行 `gh`、`git` 和捆绑的 Python 帮助程序。没有这些（一些沙盒 GUI 环境）的宿主无法运行此技能 - 说出来并停止而不是半运行。
 
-## Step 1: Confirm GitHub, resolve the PR, pick an execution mode
+## 步骤1：确认GitHub，解析PR，选择执行模式
 
-**GitHub only.** This skill and everything it delegates to speak GitHub's API (`gh`, review threads, Actions). First confirm the repo is on GitHub: `gh repo view` succeeding is the positive signal (it also covers GitHub Enterprise that `gh` is configured for). If it fails, inspect the remote — `git remote get-url origin` pointing at a `gitlab.*` host means GitLab, `bitbucket.*` means Bitbucket. On any non-GitHub forge (git hosting service), or if `gh` cannot resolve the repo at all, **stop and tell the user ce-babysit-pr is GitHub-only** and that GitLab/other forges are not yet supported. Do not proceed into `gh` calls that will produce confusing errors.
+**仅GitHub。** 这项技能及其代表的一切都代表讲GitHub的API（`gh`，审查线程，操作）。首先确认仓库位于GitHub：`gh repo view`成功是积极信号（它还涵盖`gh`配置的GitHub企业）。如果失败，请检查远程 — `git remote get-url origin` 指向 `gitlab.*` 主机表示 GitLab，`bitbucket.*` 表示 Bitbucket。在任何非GitHub伪造（git托管服务）上，或者如果`gh`根本无法解析存储库，**停止并告诉用户ce-babysit-pr仅是GitHub**并且尚不支持GitLab/other伪造。不要继续进行会产生混乱错误的 `gh` 调用。
 
-Then resolve the target PR from the argument (number/URL) or the current branch. If no open PR exists, report and stop. Resolve draft state with the PR. For an automatic calling-skill handoff without an explicit user watch-mode token, this check must be the plain read `gh pr view --json isDraft`, run before any bootstrap — never `snapshot --start-invocation`, which creates a new invocation and would supersede a watch a user explicitly authorized on that draft. A draft target reports its draft status and stops here, before any bootstrap or watcher, per the "Draft PRs are opt-in" boundary. On user-invoked runs the first snapshot's emitted `pr_is_draft` serves as the ongoing signal.
